In this research, we introduce a specific equivalence relation based on Gray classes and develop corresponding rewriting techniques. Additionally, we classify and discuss the consistency status of theories involving specific forms of commutativity, highlighting a distinct distinction between the cases of commutativity in equations and in equations with variables. Furthermore, we investigate the computational properties of relevant decision problems and establish a key finding that processing queries with a specified structure can be achieved in interative (online) manner with a bound on processing time, in contrast to other situations where such a bound is absent. Moreover, we demonstrate that, in the presence of this particular structure, determining whether a given subset of statements is satisfiable does not necessarily require excessive computation. All experiments were conducted using the Verdi rewrite tool. 

