To incorporate syntax-aware decoding into Neural Machine Translation systems, a novel method utilizing a syntactic parser has been developed to generate phrasal parsing representations in parallel with NMT outputs during decoding.
The obtained phrasal parsing representations retain "mother-daughter" structural relationships and can be further leverated as "syntactic links" to enhance NMT model performance.
Two key innovations include syntactic-aware decoding with "syntactic guides" and the utilization of "syntactic links" as additional decoding informaiton.
Experimental evaluations on English-to-German and Chinese-to-English NMT tasks have demonstrated the proposed method's superiority, with an improvement in terms of BLEU scores, being most evident in tasks with high syntax-related demands. Furthermore, the method has also achieved promising results in tree structured parsing tasks, offering a new research perspective. To facilitate future research, the proposed method's code has been made publicly available at https://github.com/GuiBrodeel/Top-Down-Tree-Structured-Decoding. 

